{"id":"mahabharata-7-057","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":57,"title":"सप्तपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 57 · Arjuna's dream of Shiva","summary":{"en":"Arjuna, in a dream, is taken by Krishna to a mountain where they praise Shiva. Shiva grants Arjuna the Pashupata weapon for his task, and they return to the camp.","kn":"ಕನಸಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ಪರ್ವತಕ್ಕೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವರು ಶಿವನನ್ನು ಸ್ತುತಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಶಿವನು ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಪಾಶುಪತಾಸ್ತ್ರವನ್ನು ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವರು ಶಿಬಿರಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"स्वप्न में कृष्ण अर्जुन को एक पर्वत पर ले जाते हैं जहाँ वे शिव की स्तुति करते हैं। शिव अर्जुन को उसके कार्य के लिए पाशुपत अस्त्र देते हैं और वे शिविर लौटते हैं।","te":"కలలో కృష్ణుడు అర్జునుని పర్వతానికి తీసుకెళతాడు; వారు శివుని స్తుతిస్తారు. శివుడు అర్జునుని కార్యానికి పాశుపతాస్త్రం ఇస్తాడు; వారు శిబిరానికి తిరిగి వస్తారు.","ta":"கனவில் கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனை மலைக்கு அழைத்துச் செல்ல, இருவரும் சிவனைத் துதிக்கின்றனர். சிவன் அர்ஜுனனின் செயலுக்காகப் பாசுபதாஸ்திரம் அளிக்க, அவர்கள் பாசறைக்குத் திரும்புகின்றனர்.","ml":"സ്വപ്നത്തിൽ കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനനെ ഒരു പർവതത്തിലേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നു; അവിടെ അവർ ശിവനെ സ്തുതിക്കുന്നു. തന്റെ ദൗത്യത്തിനായി ശിവൻ അർജുനന് പാശുപതാസ്ത്രം നൽകുന്നു; പിന്നീട് അവർ പാളയത്തിലേക്ക് മടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.57; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"प्रतिज्ञापर्व","titleEn":"Pratijna Parva (Arjuna's vow)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कुन्तीपुत्रस्तु तं मन्त्रं स्मरन्नेव धनंजयः ।\nप्रतिज्ञामात्मनो रक्षन्मुमोहाचिन्त्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, son of Kunti, of unthinkable prowess, remembering that plan and guarding his own vow, fell into a swoon."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं तु शोकेन संतप्तं स्वप्ने कपिवरध्वजम् ।\nआससाद महातेजा ध्यायन्तं गरुडध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he lay burning with grief, in a dream the greatly radiant Krishna, with the Garuda banner, came to the monkey-bannered one, who was deep in thought."}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रत्युत्थानं तु कृष्णस्य सर्वावस्थं धनंजयः ।\nनालोपयत धर्मात्मा भक्त्या प्रेम्णा च सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, righteous and always devoted and loving, never failed to rise for Krishna in any state."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रत्युत्थाय च गोविन्दं स तस्मायासनं ददौ ।\nन चासने स्वयं बुद्धिं बीभत्सुर्व्यदधात्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He rose and offered Govinda a seat, but Bibhatsu himself did not set his mind on sitting down."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः कृष्णो महातेजा जानन्पार्थस्य निश्चयम् ।\nकुन्तीपुत्रमिदं वाक्यमासीनः स्थितमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the greatly radiant Krishna, knowing Partha's resolve, seated himself and spoke to the standing son of Kunti."}},{"n":6,"text":"मा विषादे मनः पार्थ कृथाः कालो हि दुर्जयः ।\nकालः सर्वाणि भूतानि नियच्छति परे विधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Partha, do not give your mind to despair. Time is hard to conquer, and Time rules all beings under the supreme ordinance.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"किमर्थं च विषादस्ते तद्ब्रूहि वदतां वर ।\nन शोचितव्यं विदुषा शोकः कार्यविनाशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of speakers, tell me why you despair. A wise man should not grieve, for grief destroys action.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"शोचन्नन्दयते शत्रून्कर्शयत्यपि बान्धवान् ।\nक्षीयते च नरस्तस्मान्न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who grieves pleases his enemies and torments his kinsmen, and he wastes away. So you should not grieve.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"इत्युक्तो वासुदेवेन बीभत्सुरपराजितः ।\nआबभाषे तदा विद्वानिदं वचनमर्थवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Vasudeva, the unconquered Bibhatsu, who knew much, then spoke these meaningful words."}},{"n":10,"text":"मया प्रतिज्ञा महती जयद्रथवधे कृता ।\nश्वोऽस्मि हन्ता दुरात्मानं पुत्रघ्नमिति केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Keshava, I have made a great vow about Jayadratha's death: 'Tomorrow I shall kill that evil-minded killer of my son.'\""}},{"n":11,"text":"मत्प्रतिज्ञाविघातार्थं धार्तराष्ट्रैः किलाच्युत ।\nपृष्ठतः सैन्धवः कार्यः सर्वैर्गुप्तो महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Achyuta, to thwart my vow, Dhritarashtra's sons will surely place Saindhava behind them, guarded by all their great chariot-warriors.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"दश चैका च ताः कृष्ण अक्षौहिण्यः सुदुर्जयाः ।\nप्रतिज्ञायां च हीनायां कथं जीवेत मद्विधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna, they have eleven akshauhinis, very hard to conquer. If my vow fails, how could a man like me live?\""}},{"n":13,"text":"दुःखोपायस्य मे वीर विकाङ्क्षा परिवर्तते ।\nद्रुतं च याति सविता तत एतद्ब्रवीम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hero, my longing is turned to the means of sorrow, and the sun moves fast. That is why I say this.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"शोकस्थानं तु तच्छ्रुत्वा पार्थस्य द्विजकेतनः ।\nसंस्पृश्याम्भस्ततः कृष्णः प्राङ्मुखः समवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing of Partha's cause for grief, the one with the brahmin banner, Krishna, touched water and stood facing east."}},{"n":15,"text":"इदं वाक्यं महातेजा बभाषे पुष्करेक्षणः ।\nहितार्थं पाण्डुपुत्रस्य सैन्धवस्य वधे वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The greatly radiant lotus-eyed one, resolved on the killing of Saindhava, spoke these words for Pandu's son's good."}},{"n":16,"text":"पार्थ पाशुपतं नाम परमास्त्रं सनातनम् ।\nयेन सर्वान्मृधे दैत्याञ्जघ्ने देवो महेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Partha, there is a supreme eternal weapon called Pashupata, by which the god Maheshvara killed all the Daityas in battle.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"यदि तद्विदितं तेऽद्य श्वो हन्तासि जयद्रथम् ।\nअथ ज्ञातुं प्रपद्यस्व मनसा वृषभध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you know it today, you will kill Jayadratha tomorrow. If not, turn your mind to learn it from the bull-bannered Shiva.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"तं देवं मनसा ध्यायञ्जोषमास्स्व धनंजय ।\nततस्तस्य प्रसादात्त्वं भक्तः प्राप्स्यसि तन्महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Meditate on that god in your mind and stay silent, Dhananjaya. Then by his grace, as his devotee, you will obtain that great weapon.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः कृष्णवचः श्रुत्वा संस्पृश्याम्भो धनंजयः ।\nभूमावासीन एकाग्रो जगाम मनसा भवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Krishna's words, Dhananjaya touched water, sat on the ground with a concentrated mind, and went to Bhava in thought."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः प्रणिहिते ब्राह्मे मुहूर्ते शुभलक्षणे ।\nआत्मानमर्जुनोऽपश्यद्गगने सहकेशवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, at an auspicious Brahma-muhurta, Arjuna saw himself in the sky with Keshava."}},{"n":21,"text":"ज्योतिर्भिश्च समाकीर्णं सिद्धचारणसेवितम् ।\nवायुवेगगतिः पार्थः खं भेजे सहकेशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was filled with lights and served by siddhas and charanas. Partha, moving at the speed of wind, went through the sky with Keshava."}},{"n":22,"text":"केशवेन गृहीतः स दक्षिणे विभुना भुजे ।\nप्रेक्षमाणो बहून्भावाञ्जगामाद्भुतदर्शनान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Held by the lord Keshava by his right arm, he travelled, seeing many wonderful sights."}},{"n":23,"text":"उदीच्यां दिशि धर्मात्मा सोऽपश्यच्छ्वेतपर्वतम् ।\nकुबेरस्य विहारे च नलिनीं पद्मभूषिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the northern direction the righteous Arjuna saw the White Mountain and Kubera's pleasure ground with its lotus-adorned pool."}},{"n":24,"text":"सरिच्छ्रेष्ठां च तां गङ्गां वीक्षमाणो बहूदकाम् ।\nसदापुष्पफलैर्वृक्षैरुपेतां स्फटिकोपलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the Ganga, best of rivers, full of water, with trees always bearing flowers and fruit, and crystal stones."}},{"n":25,"text":"सिंहव्याघ्रसमाकीर्णां नानामृगगणाकुलाम् ।\nपुण्याश्रमवतीं रम्यां मनोज्ञाण्डजसेविताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was filled with lions and tigers, crowded with herds of many animals, lovely with holy hermitages and visited by charming birds."}},{"n":26,"text":"मन्दरस्य प्रदेशांश्च किंनरोद्गीतनादितान् ।\nहेमरूप्यमयैः शृङ्गैर्नानौषधिविदीपितान् ।\nतथा मन्दारवृक्षैश्च पुष्पितैरुपशोभितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the regions of Mandara echoing with the songs of Kinnaras, lit by many herbs on peaks of gold and silver, and adorned with blossoming mandara trees."}},{"n":27,"text":"स्निग्धाञ्जनचयाकारं संप्राप्तः कालपर्वतम् ।\nपुण्यं हिमवतः पादं मणिमन्तं च पर्वतम् ।\nब्रह्मतुङ्गं नदीश्चान्यास्तथा जनपदानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He came to the Kala mountain, which looked like a heap of glossy collyrium, the holy foot of the Himalaya, the Manimat mountain, Brahmatunga, and other rivers and countries."}},{"n":28,"text":"सुशृङ्गं शतशृङ्गं च शर्यातिवनमेव च ।\nपुण्यमश्वशिरःस्थानं स्थानमाथर्वणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw Sushringa, Shatashringa, the forest of Sharyati, the holy place of Ashvashiras, and the abode of Atharvan."}},{"n":29,"text":"वृषदंशं च शैलेन्द्रं महामन्दरमेव च ।\nअप्सरोभिः समाकीर्णं किंनरैश्चोपशोभितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw Vrishadamsha, the lord of mountains, and great Mandara, crowded with apsaras and adorned with Kinnaras."}},{"n":30,"text":"तांश्च शैलान्व्रजन्पार्थः प्रेक्षते सहकेशवः ।\nशुभैः प्रस्रवणैर्जुष्टान्हेमधातुविभूषितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going on, Partha with Keshava saw those mountains, visited by lovely streams and adorned with gold ores."}},{"n":31,"text":"चन्द्ररश्मिप्रकाशाङ्गीं पृथिवीं पुरमालिनीम् ।\nसमुद्रांश्चाद्भुताकारानपश्यद्बहुलाकरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the earth, its body bright with moonbeams and garlanded with cities, and wondrous oceans rich in many treasures."}},{"n":32,"text":"वियद्द्यां पृथिवीं चैव पश्यन्विष्णुपदे व्रजन् ।\nविस्मितः सह कृष्णेन क्षिप्तो बाण इवात्यगात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing along Vishnu's path and seeing sky, heaven and earth, he went on, amazed, with Krishna, like an arrow shot."}},{"n":33,"text":"ग्रहनक्षत्रसोमानां सूर्याग्न्योश्च समत्विषम् ।\nअपश्यत तदा पार्थो ज्वलन्तमिव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha then saw a blazing mountain, shining like the planets, stars, moon, sun and fire together."}},{"n":34,"text":"समासाद्य तु तं शैलं शैलाग्रे समवस्थितम् ।\nतपोनित्यं महात्मानमपश्यद्वृषभध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching that mountain, he saw on its summit the great-souled bull-bannered god, ever devoted to austerity."}},{"n":35,"text":"सहस्रमिव सूर्याणां दीप्यमानं स्वतेजसा ।\nशूलिनं जटिलं गौरं वल्कलाजिनवाससम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was blazing with his own radiance like a thousand suns, with a trident, matted hair, fair of complexion, clad in bark and deerskin."}},{"n":36,"text":"नयनानां सहस्रैश्च विचित्राङ्गं महौजसम् ।\nपार्वत्या सहितं देवं भूतसंघैश्च भास्वरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His body was wondrous with thousands of eyes and he was of great might, with Parvati and with shining hosts of spirits."}},{"n":37,"text":"गीतवादित्रसंह्रादैस्ताललास्यसमन्वितम् ।\nवल्गितास्फोटितोत्क्रुष्टैः पुण्यगन्धैश्च सेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was accompanied by the sounds of song and instruments, with clapping and dancing, and served by leaping, slapping and shouting spirits and holy fragrances."}},{"n":38,"text":"स्तूयमानं स्तवैर्दिव्यैर्मुनिभिर्ब्रह्मवादिभिः ।\nगोप्तारं सर्वभूतानामिष्वासधरमच्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was praised in divine hymns by sages who speak of Brahman, the guardian of all beings, the unfailing bearer of the bow."}},{"n":39,"text":"वासुदेवस्तु तं दृष्ट्वा जगाम शिरसा क्षितिम् ।\nपार्थेन सह धर्मात्मा गृणन्ब्रह्म सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, Vasudeva bowed his head to the ground with Partha, the righteous one chanting the eternal Brahman."}},{"n":40,"text":"लोकादिं विश्वकर्माणमजमीशानमव्ययम् ।\nमनसः परमां योनिं खं वायुं ज्योतिषां निधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He praised him as the source of the worlds, the maker of all, unborn, the lord, imperishable, the highest origin of the mind, the sky, the wind and the treasury of lights."}},{"n":41,"text":"स्रष्टारं वारिधाराणां भुवश्च प्रकृतिं पराम् ।\nदेवदानवयक्षाणां मानवानां च साधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He praised him as creator of rivers of water, the supreme nature of the earth, the means of gods, danavas, yakshas and men."}},{"n":42,"text":"योगिनां परमं ब्रह्म व्यक्तं ब्रह्मविदां निधिम् ।\nचराचरस्य स्रष्टारं प्रतिहर्तारमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the supreme Brahman of yogis, the manifest treasure of Brahman-knowers, the creator and the withdrawer of the moving and unmoving."}},{"n":43,"text":"कालकोपं महात्मानं शक्रसूर्यगुणोदयम् ।\nअवन्दत तदा कृष्णो वाङ्मनोबुद्धिकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna then saluted the great-souled one, the wrath of Time, from whom arise the qualities of Indra and Surya, with speech, mind, intellect and action."}},{"n":44,"text":"यं प्रपश्यन्ति विद्वांसः सूक्ष्माध्यात्मपदैषिणः ।\nतमजं कारणात्मानं जग्मतुः शरणं भवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise who seek the subtle path of the Self behold him. The two went to that unborn Bhava, the cause of all, for refuge."}},{"n":45,"text":"अर्जुनश्चापि तं देवं भूयो भूयोऽभ्यवन्दत ।\nज्ञात्वैकं भूतभव्यादिं सर्वभूतभवोद्भवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna too bowed again and again to that god, knowing him to be the one who is the origin of past and future, and of all beings."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततस्तावागतौ शर्वः प्रोवाच प्रहसन्निव ।\nस्वागतं वां नरश्रेष्ठावुत्तिष्ठेतां गतक्लमौ ।\nकिं च वामीप्सितं वीरौ मनसः क्षिप्रमुच्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sharva, as if laughing, said to the two who had come, \"Welcome, best of men. Rise, free from weariness. Tell me quickly, heroes, what you desire in your minds.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"येन कार्येण संप्राप्तौ युवां तत्साधयामि वाम् ।\nव्रियतामात्मनः श्रेयस्तत्सर्वं प्रददानि वाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shall accomplish for you the purpose for which you have come. Choose what is best for you, and I shall give it all.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"ततस्तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा प्रत्युत्थाय कृताञ्जली ।\nवासुदेवार्जुनौ शर्वं तुष्टुवाते महामती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, Vasudeva and Arjuna, both wise, rose with joined hands and praised Sharva."}},{"n":49,"text":"नमो भवाय शर्वाय रुद्राय वरदाय च ।\nपशूनां पतये नित्यमुग्राय च कपर्दिने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Salutations to Bhava, Sharva, Rudra, giver of boons, lord of beasts, ever fierce, the one with matted locks.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"महादेवाय भीमाय त्र्यम्बकाय च शंभवे ।\nईशानाय भगघ्नाय नमोऽस्त्वन्धकघातिने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Salutations to Mahadeva, the terrible, the three-eyed, Shambhu, Ishana, destroyer of Bhaga's eyes, slayer of Andhaka.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"कुमारगुरवे नित्यं नीलग्रीवाय वेधसे ।\nविलोहिताय धूम्राय व्याधायानपराजिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Always to the teacher of Kumara, the blue-throated, the creator, the dark red, the smoke-coloured, the hunter, the unconquered.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"नित्यं नीलशिखण्डाय शूलिने दिव्यचक्षुषे ।\nहन्त्रे गोप्त्रे त्रिनेत्राय व्याधाय वसुरेतसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Always to the one with the blue crest, the trident-bearer, with divine sight, the destroyer and protector, the three-eyed hunter, with golden seed.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"अचिन्त्यायाम्बिकाभर्त्रे सर्वदेवस्तुताय च ।\nवृषध्वजाय पिङ्गाय जटिने ब्रह्मचारिणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"To the inconceivable husband of Ambika, praised by all gods, the bull-bannered, the tawny one, the matted-haired celibate.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"तप्यमानाय सलिले ब्रह्मण्यायाजिताय च ।\nविश्वात्मने विश्वसृजे विश्वमावृत्य तिष्ठते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"To him who practises austerity in water, who is devoted to brahmins and unconquered, the soul of the universe, maker of the universe, who stands pervading the universe.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"नमो नमस्ते सेव्याय भूतानां प्रभवे सदा ।\nब्रह्मवक्त्राय शर्वाय शंकराय शिवाय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Again and again salutations to him who is to be served, the lord of beings, the one with Brahma's face, Sharva, Shankara and Shiva.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"नमोऽस्तु वाचस्पतये प्रजानां पतये नमः ।\nनमो विश्वस्य पतये महतां पतये नमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Salutations to the lord of speech, to the lord of creatures, to the lord of the universe, to the lord of the great.\""}},{"n":57,"text":"नमः सहस्रशिरसे सहस्रभुजमन्यवे ।\nसहस्रनेत्रपादाय नमोऽसंख्येयकर्मणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Salutations to him of a thousand heads, of thousand arms and fury, of a thousand eyes and feet, whose deeds are countless.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"नमो हिरण्यवर्णाय हिरण्यकवचाय च ।\nभक्तानुकम्पिने नित्यं सिध्यतां नौ वरः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Salutations to him of golden colour and golden armour, ever kind to devotees. Lord, let our boon be accomplished.\""}},{"n":59,"text":"एवं स्तुत्वा महादेवं वासुदेवः सहार्जुनः ।\nप्रसादयामास भवं तदा ह्यस्त्रोपलब्धये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having praised Mahadeva thus, Vasudeva with Arjuna then propitiated Bhava to obtain the weapon."}},{"n":60,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनः प्रीतमना ववन्दे वृषभध्वजम् ।\nददर्शोत्फुल्लनयनः समस्तं तेजसां निधिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, delighted, saluted the bull-bannered one and, with eyes wide, saw him as the whole treasury of splendours."}},{"n":61,"text":"तं चोपहारं स्वकृतं नैशं नैत्यकमात्मनः ।\nददर्श त्र्यम्बकाभ्याशे वासुदेवनिवेदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw near Tryambaka that same night offering he himself had made, which Vasudeva had presented."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततोऽभिपूज्य मनसा शर्वं कृष्णं च पाण्डवः ।\nइच्छाम्यहं दिव्यमस्त्रमित्यभाषत शंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, honouring Sharva and Krishna in his mind, the Pandava said to Shankara, \"I desire the divine weapon.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"ततः पार्थस्य विज्ञाय वरार्थे वचनं प्रभुः ।\nवासुदेवार्जुनौ देवः स्मयमानोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding Partha's words asking for a boon, the lord, smiling, said to Vasudeva and Arjuna."}},{"n":64,"text":"सरोऽमृतमयं दिव्यमभ्याशे शत्रुसूदनौ ।\nतत्र मे तद्धनुर्दिव्यं शरश्च निहितः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nearby, destroyers of foes, there is a divine lake of nectar. There, long ago, I placed my divine bow and arrow.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"येन देवारयः सर्वे मया युधि निपातिताः ।\nतत आनीयतां कृष्णौ सशरं धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By them I struck down all the enemies of the gods in battle. Go, you two, and bring from there that excellent bow with its arrow.\""}},{"n":66,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा तु तौ वीरौ तं शर्वं पार्षदैः सह ।\nप्रस्थितौ तत्सरो दिव्यं दिव्याश्चर्यशतैर्वृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" the two heroes, with Sharva and his attendants, set out to that divine lake, surrounded by hundreds of divine wonders."}},{"n":67,"text":"निर्दिष्टं यद्वृषाङ्केन पुण्यं सर्वार्थसाधकम् ।\nतज्जग्मतुरसंभ्रान्तौ नरनारायणावृषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two sages, Nara and Narayana, unperturbed, went to that holy lake pointed out by the bull-marked one, which accomplishes every aim."}},{"n":68,"text":"ततस्तु तत्सरो गत्वा सूर्यमण्डलसंनिभम् ।\nनागमन्तर्जले घोरं ददृशातेऽर्जुनाच्युतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrived at that lake, bright as the sun's disc, Arjuna and Achyuta saw a terrible serpent in the water."}},{"n":69,"text":"द्वितीयं चापरं नागं सहस्रशिरसं वरम् ।\nवमन्तं विपुलां ज्वालां ददृशातेऽग्निवर्चसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They also saw a second excellent serpent with a thousand heads, fire-bright and vomiting vast flames."}},{"n":70,"text":"ततः कृष्णश्च पार्थश्च संस्पृश्यापः कृताञ्जली ।\nतौ नागावुपतस्थाते नमस्यन्तौ वृषध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna and Partha touched water, joined their hands, and approached those two serpents, bowing to the bull-bannered god."}},{"n":71,"text":"गृणन्तौ वेदविदुषौ तद्ब्रह्म शतरुद्रियम् ।\nअप्रमेयं प्रणमन्तौ गत्वा सर्वात्मना भवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the Vedas, they recited that Brahman hymn, the Shatarudriya, and bowed to the immeasurable Bhava, approaching him with their whole selves."}},{"n":72,"text":"ततस्तौ रुद्रमाहात्म्याद्धित्वा रूपं महोरगौ ।\nधनुर्बाणश्च शत्रुघ्नं तद्द्वंद्वं समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, by the greatness of Rudra, those two great serpents gave up their forms and became that pair, the bow and the arrow, destroyers of foes."}},{"n":73,"text":"ततो जगृहतुः प्रीतौ धनुर्बाणं च सुप्रभम् ।\nआजह्रतुर्महात्मानौ ददतुश्च महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two great-souled ones, pleased, took the bright bow and arrow, brought them, and gave them to the great-souled Shiva."}},{"n":74,"text":"ततः पार्श्वाद्वृषाङ्कस्य ब्रह्मचारी न्यवर्तत ।\nपिङ्गाक्षस्तपसः क्षेत्रं बलवान्नीललोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from the side of the bull-marked one came a celibate student, tawny-eyed, strong and dark-red, the field of austerity."}},{"n":75,"text":"स तद्गृह्य धनुःश्रेष्ठं तस्थौ स्थानं समाहितः ।\nव्यकर्षच्चापि विधिवत्सशरं धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took that excellent bow and stood steadily in his place, and drew the excellent bow with its arrow, as is prescribed."}},{"n":76,"text":"तस्य मौर्वीं च मुष्टिं च स्थानं चालक्ष्य पाण्डवः ।\nश्रुत्वा मन्त्रं भवप्रोक्तं जग्राहाचिन्त्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Observing his bowstring, his grip and his stance, the Pandava of unthinkable valour took in the mantra spoken by Bhava."}},{"n":77,"text":"सरस्येव च तं बाणं मुमोचातिबलः प्रभुः ।\nचकार च पुनर्वीरस्तस्मिन्सरसि तद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty lord released that arrow into the lake itself, and the hero then put that bow back in that lake."}},{"n":78,"text":"ततः प्रीतं भवं ज्ञात्वा स्मृतिमानर्जुनस्तदा ।\nवरमारण्यकं दत्तं दर्शनं शंकरस्य च ।\nमनसा चिन्तयामास तन्मे संपद्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knowing Bhava to be pleased, Arjuna, remembering, thought in his mind that the boon of living in the forest and the sight of Shankara given earlier should be fulfilled for him."}},{"n":79,"text":"तस्य तन्मतमाज्ञाय प्रीतः प्रादाद्वरं भवः ।\nतच्च पाशुपतं घोरं प्रतिज्ञायाश्च पारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing his wish, Bhava, pleased, gave him the boon: that terrible Pashupata weapon and the fulfilment of his vow."}},{"n":80,"text":"संहृष्टरोमा दुर्धर्षः कृतं कार्यममन्यत ।\nववन्दतुश्च संहृष्टौ शिरोभ्यां तौ महेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With hair bristling with joy, the unassailable one felt his task done. Both, delighted, bowed their heads to Maheshvara."}},{"n":81,"text":"अनुज्ञातौ क्षणे तस्मिन्भवेनार्जुनकेशवौ ।\nप्राप्तौ स्वशिबिरं वीरौ मुदा परमया युतौ ।\nइन्द्राविष्णू यथा प्रीतौ जम्भस्य वधकाङ्क्षिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Given leave at that moment by Bhava, the heroes Arjuna and Keshava reached their own camp, filled with supreme joy, like Indra and Vishnu pleased and wishing to kill Jambha."}}]}]}